// S441 reproducer — addendum item 23: the retired `@debounced(N) <x> = …` form compiles clean and the
// declaration is never emitted.
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/retired-debounced-decorator-silently-dropped.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: a diagnostic. §6.13 (SPEC.md:~5958): the `debounced=` attribute "Supersedes the pre-v0.next
//           `@debounced(N) name = expr` keyword-form modifier surface (deleted at S79 …)". The canonical form is
//           `<slow debounced=300ms> = @query`.
// Actual:   the declaration is dropped with no diagnostic of its own. When the only read sits inside an arrow
//           body (the onboarding probe k0/k43 shape, reproduced here) the compile is exit 0 with zero
//           diagnostics and client.js reads a cell nobody declares or sets
//           (`… .filter((w) => w.includes(_scrml_cs_reactive_get("slow")))`) — here that silently searches for
//           the string "undefined"; k43's `.toLowerCase()` on it throws. With a direct read
//           (`const <shown> = @slow.toLowerCase()`) it instead fails E-STATE-UNDECLARED — loud, but naming the
//           wrong cause (the declaration was written and silently discarded).
<program>
${
  <query> = ""
  @debounced(300) <slow> = @query
  const words = ["apple", "banana"]
  const <shown> = words.filter(w => w.includes(@slow))
}
<input bind:value=@query/>
<p>${@shown.length}</p>
</program>
